PR #3 added a _bytes attribute meant to hold the header bytes read from the file, but parse_from_fh passed the constructor key "bytes" while Moo init_arg was "_bytes", so the value was silently dropped and verify_mac fell back to the lazy builder, i.e. to the re-serialization of the parsed stanzas. Measured before the fix: 0 builder calls after parse, 1 after MAC verify.

Fixed by passing _bytes => $bytes, matching the attribute name. Read path now MACs what the file actually contained; write path is untouched and still serializes via the builder.

Deliberate wire change - the option skill crypt-age-core describes as "a parse-time capture of the literal header bytes would remove the coupling". Verified with age 1.1.1: both directions at 0/1/65535/65536/65537/131072 bytes with 1 and 3 recipients, and a hand-built spec-legal header that age accepts, the old code rejected and the new code accepts.

In the working tree of branch integrate-filehandle, not yet committed.
Implemented on branch integrate-filehandle; diff awaiting maintainer review before commit. Regression tests for the literal-bytes capture are not written yet - that is test-writer work.
